# Local development variables for the public Worker.
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars`, which is git-ignored, and fill in the values.
#
# Cloudflare does not read this file in production: upload Worker secrets with
# `wrangler secret put` and put plain variables under `[env.production.vars]` in
# wrangler.toml.

# Required for keyed network hashing and for poll/comment ownership. Any 64-character
# hex value works locally (`openssl rand -hex 32`). Without it the health endpoint
# reports `serverKey: false`, and voting, registration, sign-in, poll submission, and
# comments return `503`.
#
# WARNING - SAVE THIS VALUE. Cloudflare never displays a stored Worker secret again,
# so the production value has to be kept somewhere you control (a password manager or a
# secret vault). Losing it is not just an outage: every stored poll and comment owner
# hash is derived from this key, so after a different key is deployed no existing poll
# or comment can ever be matched to its author again ("my polls" and "my comments" go
# empty, and close, withdraw, and delete refuse for that content). Generate one value,
# store it, and reuse the same value in production, on every new account, and locally.
# See docs/RUNBOOK.md, "Migrating to another Cloudflare account".
SERVER_HMAC_KEY=

# Optional Turnstile. The widget and the server-side check are skipped while either
# value is empty, so leave both blank for normal local development. Set both to test
# the widget against a real Turnstile key pair; Turnstile is enabled exactly when
# both are present.
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
